# An Omen's "shuffles it into its owner's library instead of putting it into its owner's graveyard as it resolves" (CR 720.3d)
# is a replacement effect (CR 614.1a), ordered by the spell's controller with the others that would change the move (CR
# 616.1). Bot2 begins with Leyline of the Void ("If a card would be put into an opponent's graveyard from anywhere, exile it
# instead"). On turn 3 Bot1 Brainstorms, putting a Lightning Bolt and then the Plains it drew back on top, and casts Twinmaw
# Stormbrood as its Omen, Charring Bite, at Bot2's Llanowar Elves. As it resolves Bot1 takes the Leyline's exile first, to keep
# the cards it stacked: the Stormbrood is exiled (as Brainstorm was), the Omen's shuffle no longer applies (CR 616.1f), and the library is as
# Brainstorm left it, the Plains and then the Bolt on top.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Twinmaw Stormbrood
Brainstorm
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Plains
Forest
Swamp
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Leyline of the Void
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x17

